{"name":"Medium Candy Apple Red","hex":"#e2062c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"medium","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The material of the surrounding environment, e.g. solid, liquid, gas, vacuum, or a specific substance such as a solvent.","The materials or empty space through which signals, waves, or forces pass."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["One of several common sizes to which an item may be manufactured, smaller than a large but larger than a small.","An item labelled or denoted as being that size."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/medium"},{"term":"candy","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Crystallized sugar formed by boiling down sugar syrup.","Edible, sweet-tasting confectionery containing sugar, or sometimes artificial sweeteners, and often flavored with fruit, chocolate, nuts, herbs and spices, or artificial flavors."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cook in or coat with sugar syrup.","To form into congelations or crystals, especially of sugar or syrup."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/candy"},{"term":"apple","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A common, firm, round fruit produced by a tree of the genus Malus.","The fruit of the tree Malus domestica, chiefly with a green, red, or yellow skin, cultivated in temperate climates for cidermaking, cooking, and eating. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make (something) appear like an apple (noun sense 1.1).","To become like an apple.\n\n To collect fir-cones.\n Of a flower bud or vegetable (especially a root vegetable): to grow into the shape of an apple."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/apple"}],"entries":[{"title":"Candy apple red","blocks":[{"text":"Candy apple red is the name code used by manufacturing companies to define a shade of red similar to the red sugar coating on candied apples. The typical method for producing a candy apple finish is to apply a metallic base-coat, followed by a translucent color coat. A final clear coat adds additional gloss."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy_apple_red","wikidata":"Q13631176"},{"title":"Candy apple","blocks":[{"text":"Candy apples or toffee apples are whole apples covered in a sugar candy coating, with a stick inserted as a handle. These are a common treat at fall festivals in Western culture in the Northern Hemisphere, such as Halloween and Guy Fawkes Night, because these festivals occur in the wake of annual apple harvests. Although candy apples and caramel apples may seem similar, they are made using distinctly different processes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ad/Tastee-Candy-Apple-Red-Caramel-wPeanuts.jpg/330px-Tastee-Candy-Apple-Red-Caramel-wPeanuts.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy_apple","wikidata":"Q1358074"},{"title":"Candy","blocks":[{"text":"Candy, also known as sweets and lollies, is a confection that features sugar as a principal ingredient. The category, sugar confectionery, encompasses any sweet confection, including chocolate or chewing gum. Sugar-glazed vegetables, fruit, or nuts are considered candied."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/10/Candy_in_Damascus.jpg/330px-Candy_in_Damascus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Candy","wikidata":"Q185583"},{"title":"Apple","blocks":[{"text":"An apple is the round, edible fruit of an apple tree. Fruit trees of the orchard or domestic apple, the most widely grown in the genus, are cultivated worldwide. The tree originated in Central Asia, where its wild ancestor, Malus sieversii, is still found. Apples have been grown for thousands of years in Eurasia before they were introduced to the American continent by European colonists. Apples have cultural significance in many mythologies and religions."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a6/Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg/330px-Pink_lady_and_cross_section.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple","wikidata":"Q89"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Harley-Davidson_Museum_Easy_Rider_Captain_America_Bike.JPG/500px-Harley-Davidson_Museum_Easy_Rider_Captain_America_Bike.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Harley-Davidson_Museum_Easy_Rider_Captain_America_Bike.JPG/1280px-Harley-Davidson_Museum_Easy_Rider_Captain_America_Bike.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3b/Harley-Davidson_Museum_Easy_Rider_Captain_America_Bike.JPG/500px-Harley-Davidson_Museum_Easy_Rider_Captain_America_Bike.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Billy Bike Harley Chopper in Easy Rider was painted in candy apple red with a flame design on the tear drop gas tank","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHarley-Davidson_Museum_Easy_Rider_Captain_America_Bike.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Pommes_d_amour.jpg/500px-Pommes_d_amour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Pommes_d_amour.jpg/1280px-Pommes_d_amour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Pommes_d_amour.jpg/500px-Pommes_d_amour.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pommes d'amour on display","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APommes_d_amour.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.